   "text": {
    "L1": "Saving energy starts with small actions at home.",
    "L2": "A common myth says switching off appliances makes no real difference. That is not true.",
    "L3": "Much of India's electricity is made by burning coal, which will run out and pollutes the air.",
    "L4": "When we use less electricity, power stations need to burn less coal. Small savings from many homes add up.",
    "L5": "Use daylight, switch off lights and fans when leaving, and choose LED bulbs.",
    "L6": "Switch TVs and chargers off at the wall, keep the fridge door closed, and walk or cycle when you can.",
    "L7": "Now choose the action that saves electricity when nobody is using the room."
   },
